error[E0277]: `IntentRow` rows are the platform's, and app code cannot write them
  --> tests/compile_fail/intent_row_written_on_bare_tx.rs:13:12
   |
13 |     tx.put(row);
   |        --- ^^^ `IntentRow` is written only by the platform
   |        |
   |        required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `AppWritable<IntentRow>` is not implemented for `charpente::charpente_core::table::PlatformOwned`
   = note: job rows are the platform's: only the enqueue family writes one, so a job runs in the tenant its enqueuer opened or its fan-out named, and no app code cancels one — to run a job, enqueue it:
               tx.enqueue(job);
           for a `global` job; for a `scoped_by` job, inside the tenant it acts in:
               let mut tx = tx.scope::<Org>(scope, ctx)?;
               tx.enqueue(job);
           or from a `cross_tenant` route or job, naming the tenant:
               tx.enqueue_in::<Org>(scope, job, cap);
   = note: event rows are the platform's: only an emit writes one, because every subscription's feed is read from them — to publish an event, emit it with `tx.emit(event)`, or, inside a tenant, with `emit` on the `ScopedTx` of the tenant it belongs to
   = note: schema-version rows are the platform's: only a table's first write and `Db::migrate_schema` write one, because the migration gate trusts them for each table's version and a migration's resume point — to change a table's version, declare it with `#[table(version = N)]` and its `TableMigration`, and the kernel migrates at startup
   = note: intent rows are the platform's: only the request path writes one, in the transaction of the write it records, because a re-sent request is answered from it without running — charpente records each write route's reply itself, so there is nothing to write; a handler that remembers an id of its own keeps it in a table of the app's own
help: the trait `AppWritable<R>` is implemented for `Unscoped`
  --> $WORKSPACE/crates/charpente-core/src/table.rs
   |
   | impl<R> AppWritable<R> for Unscoped {}
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: required for `IntentRow` to implement `WritableRow`
note: required by a bound in `Tx::<'a>::put`
